# amsterdank — MOOLLM-compatible application repo
# Pointers only. The conventions live upstream; this file says where.

repo: amsterdank
moollm_compatible: true
upstream: "https://github.com/SimHacker/moollm"

rules:

  - name: boot-sequence
    description: "Start here when entering amsterdank."
    steps:
      - "Read skills/INDEX.yml — what is local, what is inherited from moollm."
      - "Read sources.yml — every source, its license, its osm_ok flag. Nothing is fetched or trusted without an entry here."
      - "Read skills/coffeeshop/GLANCE.yml, then CARD.yml, then SKILL.md only if authoring."
      - "For place/room/budtender conventions, read them in the moollm repo. Do not vendor copies."

  - name: yaml-is-the-truth
    description: "Direction of authority is one-way."
    rules:
      - "places/<id>/PLACE.yml is canonical. data/*.csv and any database are DERIVED."
      - "Never hand-edit a derived file. Regenerate it."
      - "Generators PROPOSE and never overwrite hand-written YAML comments. The comments are the fieldwork."

  - name: provenance-has-teeth
    description: "Two legal directions, enforced structurally. See LICENSE-DATA."
    rules:
      - "Every value carries source, observed date, and confidence. A value without provenance is not data."
      - "osm_ok: false sources may NEVER reach an OSM changeset. No exceptions for convenience."
      - "OSM material stays in data/osm/, referenced by ID, never merged into PLACE.yml — ODbL share-alike would swallow the repo."
      - "Nothing here writes to OSM. Findings leave as a worklist a human types into an editor."
      - "Third-party compilations are gitignored. An EU database right can protect the collection even when the facts are free."

  - name: keep-the-disagreement
    description: "Conflicts are the interesting part."
    rules:
      - "Claims accumulate; they are never replaced. Resolution happens at read time, reversibly."
      - "Never average two coordinates. The mean of two buildings is a canal."
      - "Absence means unknown, never false."
      - "'Illegible' is a legitimate value and schedules a revisit. A guess is not."

  - name: menus-stay-polymorphic
    description: "Each shop's board is its own ontology."
    rules:
      - "Keep the shop's categories, labels, capitals and Dutch verbatim. Project to the shared vocabulary; never rewrite into it."
      - "Keep the unit as sold. A fixed-price bag has no gram price, and computing one is fabrication with a decimal point."

  - name: no-decorative-comments
    description: "Inherited from moollm. Comments must add meaning."
    forbidden: ["# ═══════", "# ───────", "# =======", "# -------"]
